      {
        "title": "Cucumber",
        "properties": {
          "cucumber.features": {
            "markdownDescription": "The `cucumber.features` setting overrides where the extension\nshould look for `.feature` files.\n\nIf no feature files are found, [autocomplete](#autocomplete)\nwill not work.\n\nDefault value:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"cucumber.features\": [\n    \"src/test/**/*.feature\",\n    \"features/**/*.feature\",\n    \"tests/**/*.feature\",\n    \"*specs*/**/*.feature\"\n  ]\n}\n```",
            "type": "array",
            "required": false,
            "default": [
              "src/test/**/*.feature",
              "features/**/*.feature",
              "tests/**/*.feature",
              "*specs*/**/*.feature"
            ]
          },
          "cucumber.glue": {
            "markdownDescription": "The `cucumber.glue` setting overrides where the extension\nshould look for source code where step definitions and\nparameter types are defined.\n\nIf no glue files are found, [autocomplete](#autocomplete)\nwill not work, and all Gherkin steps will be underlined as\nundefined. [Generate step definition](#generate-step-definition)\nwill not work either.\n\nDefault value:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"cucumber.glue\": [\n    \"*specs*/**/*.cs\",\n    \"features/**/*.js\",\n    \"features/**/*.jsx\",\n    \"features/**/*.php\",\n    \"features/**/*.py\",\n    \"features/**/*.rs\",\n    \"features/**/*.rb\",\n    \"features/**/*.ts\",\n    \"features/**/*.tsx\",\n    \"features/**/*_test.go\",\n    \"src/test/**/*.java\",\n    \"tests/**/*.py\",\n    \"tests/**/*.rs\",\n    \"**/steps/**/*.py\",\n    \"steps/**/*.py\",\n    \"**/*_steps.py\",\n    \"**/step_*.py\",\n    \"**/steps.py\"\n  ]\n}\n```",
            "type": "array",
            "required": false,
            "default": [
              "*specs*/**/*.cs",
              "features/**/*.js",
              "features/**/*.jsx",
              "features/**/*.php",
              "features/**/*.py",
              "features/**/*.rs",
              "features/**/*.rb",
              "features/**/*.ts",
              "features/**/*.tsx",
              "features/**/*_test.go",
              "src/test/**/*.java",
              "tests/**/*.py",
              "tests/**/*.rs",
              "**/steps/**/*.py",
              "steps/**/*.py",
              "**/*_steps.py",
              "**/step_*.py",
              "**/steps.py"
            ]
          },
          "cucumber.parameterTypes": {
            "markdownDescription": "Override the `cucumber.parameterTypes` setting if your Cucumber Expressions\nare using [Custom Parameter Types](https://github.com/cucumber/cucumber-expressions#custom-parameter-types) that are defined outside your `cucumber.glue` setting.\n\nParameter Types in the `cucumber.glue` globs will be picked up automatically.\n\nDefault value:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"cucumber.parameterTypes\": []\n}\n```",
            "type": "array",
            "required": false,
            "default": []
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Smart Cucumber-Behave: Gherkin Formatter",
        "properties": {
          "smartBehave.formatting.customIndent.enabled": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": true,
            "description": "Enable custom fine-grained Gherkin indentation per keyword (Feature, Scenario, Background, Given, When, Then, And, But)"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indentCharacter": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "auto",
              "tab",
              "spaces"
            ],
            "default": "auto",
            "description": "Indentation character unit: 'tab' forces tabs ('\\t'), 'spaces' uses editor tabSize spaces, 'auto' respects VS Code editor settings"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.feature": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 0,
            "description": "Indentation level (number of tabs/indents) for Feature: headers (e.g. 0 tabs = no tab)"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.scenario": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 1,
            "description": "Indentation level for Scenario: and Scenario Outline: headers (e.g. 1 tab after Feature)"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.background": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 1,
            "description": "Indentation level for Background: headers"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.rule": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 1,
            "description": "Indentation level for Rule: headers"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.examples": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 2,
            "description": "Indentation level for Examples: headers"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.given": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 2,
            "description": "Indentation level for Given steps (e.g. 2 tabs = one more tab after Scenario)"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.when": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 2,
            "description": "Indentation level for When steps"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.then": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 3,
            "description": "Indentation level for Then steps (e.g. 3 tabs = one more tab after Given)"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.and": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 4,
            "description": "Indentation level for And steps (e.g. 4 tabs = one more tab after Then)"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.but": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 4,
            "description": "Indentation level for But steps"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.indent.star": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 2,
            "description": "Indentation level for * (wildcard) steps"
          },
          "smartBehave.formatting.relativeAnd": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": false,
            "description": "If true, And/But steps are indented relative to the preceding step (+1 tab); if false, uses explicit and/but tab levels"
          }
        }
      }
